Request: Enter the Globex invoice that arrived as a scanned copy.
Understanding the request (reading relevant SOPs)…
Contract:
REQUEST: Enter the Globex invoice that arrived as a scanned copy.
INTENDED OUTCOME: Record the Globex invoice that arrived in the AP mailbox as a scanned copy into the ERP as a bill, without creating a duplicate or making 
unrelated changes.
DELIVERABLE TO USER: Confirmation to the requester with either the new ERP bill ID or the existing duplicate bill ID, plus extracted invoice fields and evidence
from both the ERP and the mailbox.
CONSTRAINTS:
  - Use ERP read-only API endpoints for all lookups; perform all ERP writes via the GUI only.
  - Check for an existing bill by Globex vendor and extracted invoice number before recording.
  - Do not create or edit vendors; only record the bill if the Globex vendor already exists in the ERP.
  - Do not initiate or schedule payments; only enter the invoice as a bill.
  - Do not alter unrelated ERP records.
  - Do not guess missing or illegible invoice fields; stop and report if required data cannot be extracted.
  - Keep the original email and downloaded scanned attachment as evidence.
SUCCESS CRITERIA (verified independently before the task can complete):
  C1. Exactly one ERP bill exists for the scanned Globex invoice, identified by the extracted invoice number under the correct Globex vendor; if it already 
existed before this task, no new bill was created.
  C2. The entered or existing bill's vendor, invoice number, invoice date, currency, and total amount match the scanned document.
  C3. No unintended ERP changes occurred: no new vendor created, no payment scheduled, and other bills unchanged.
  C4. The requester receives a report with the bill ID (new or existing), extracted fields, and evidence of the duplicate check.
ASSUMPTIONS:
  - The scanned invoice is in the AP shared mailbox as an attachment and is the only Globex scanned invoice currently being requested.
  - Globex corresponds to a single existing ERP vendor; if multiple Globex vendors exist, the one referenced by the email sender/domain will be used or the 
ambiguity will be reported.
  - All invoice fields needed for bill entry are legible from the scanned copy.
  - ERP write actions may be approval-gated by the platform; the operator will attempt the GUI write and the platform will request approval if policy requires 
it.
PLAN:
  S1: Look up the Globex vendor and any existing Globex bills in the ERP to establish a baseline and obtain the vendor ID using read-only APIs. (done when: GET 
/vendors?q=Globex returns a unique vendor ID or the missing/ambiguous vendor state is captured, and existing bills for that vendor are listed.)
  S2: Locate the scanned Globex invoice email in the AP shared mailbox (ap@kestrel.in). (done when: A candidate email is identified in /mail whose 
sender/subject indicates Globex and which has at least one scanned attachment.)
  S3: Download the scanned attachment from that email into the run workspace. (done when: The attachment file exists in the local drive and can be opened under 
the workspace.)
  S4: Extract invoice data from the scanned document. (done when: Invoice number, invoice date, total amount, currency, and vendor name are captured; any 
missing critical field is recorded as a blocker.)
  S5: Check the ERP for an existing bill using the identified vendor ID and extracted invoice number. (done when: GET 
/bills?vendor_id=<vendor_id>&invoice_number=<invoice_number> returns either zero or exactly one existing bill.)
  S6: Record the bill in the ERP via the GUI only if no existing bill was found; if a duplicate exists, do not create a new bill. (done when: A new bill ID is 
generated and observable in ERP, or the existing bill ID is captured and reported without any write.)
  S7: Verify the final bill state in the ERP and report the outcome to the requester. (done when: GET /bills/<bill_id> matches the extracted fields and the 
requester receives confirmation with evidence.)
